Just a little off-topic correction here...

"Strongness" of acids is no measure for the described effect. The effect
is based on the H2SO4/H2O configuration, where the heat from the specific
hydration effect immediately boils the water and thus spreads the acid
with the water (the boiling water carries acid with it). If, the other
way round, you put the sulfuric acid slowly into the water while stirring
the water the hydration energy can disseminate in the water. (The boiling
point of sulfuric acid is much higher than water at ~330 deg Celsius.)

So assuming Nethack's acid could be sulfuric acid; dipping a wooden staff
(or other wooden or organic material) into it should dehydrate the object
turning it black (if wooden) or make it rot (if clothen). YANI, I guess,
currently no such effect can be observed in Nethack. Though the effect on
cloth could be easily implemented, and also the effect on wooden objects,
since the "burnt" attribute is usable (burning is just dehydration in the
first stage).

